  "body": {
    "id": "lem:finite-honest-confidence",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For every finite revealed graph \\(G\\), every \\(0<\\alpha<1\\), and every \\(y\\in\\mathcal M_n(G)\\), the selected certified procedure satisfies\n\\[\n\\Pr_{\\mathcal D_G}\\!\\left\\{\\tau_n\\in\\mathcal C_\\alpha(G,Z,Y^{\\mathrm{obs}})\\mid G\\right\\}\\ge1-\\alpha.\n\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "G",
      "\\alpha",
      "y",
      "\\mathcal M_n(G)",
      "\\mathcal D_G",
      "\\tau_n",
      "\\mathcal C_\\alpha(G,Z,Y^{\\mathrm{obs}})",
      "Z",
      "Y^{\\mathrm{obs}}"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:outcome-class",
      "def:certified-procedure",
      "def:confidence-set",
      "lem:schur-certificate"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "If the certified procedure selects the seed branch, Lemma~\\(\\mathrm{lem{:}schur\\mbox{-}certificate}\\) gives MSE at most \\(U(G,k_n)=\\overline U(G)\\).  On either fallback branch its report is \\(\\mu_1\\), its error is \\(\\mu_0\\), and the control endpoint restriction gives \\(\\mu_0^2\\le n^{-1}\\sum_i b_i^2\\le1=\\overline U(G)\\).  Thus, uniformly over \\(y\\in\\mathcal M_n(G)\\),\n\\[\n\\mathbb E_{\\mathcal D_G,y}\\!\\left[(\\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{cert}}-\\tau_n)^2\\mid G\\right]\\le\\overline U(G).\n\\tag{20}\n\\]\nBecause the squared error is nonnegative, (20) implies directly\n\\[\n\\Pr_{\\mathcal D_G}\\!\\left\\{|\\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{cert}}-\\tau_n|>\\sqrt{\\overline U(G)/\\alpha}\\,\\middle|\\,G\\right\\}\n\\le\\alpha.\n\\tag{21}\n\\]\nThe endpoint second-moment restrictions and Cauchy--Schwarz give \\(|\\mu_1|\\le1\\) and \\(|\\mu_0|\\le1\\), hence \\(\\tau_n\\in[-2,2]\\).  On the complement of the event in (21), \\(\\tau_n\\) belongs both to the untruncated interval centered at \\(\\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{cert}}\\) and to \\([-2,2]\\); it therefore belongs to their intersection \\(\\mathcal C_\\alpha(G,Z,Y^{\\mathrm{obs}})\\).  This proves the finite-sample conditional coverage claim.",
